TEXT -216 -40 Left 2 ;delta Q for all three phases is: \n-220MVAr (Q0 from lines) + 1200MVAr \n= 1420MVar = 1.42GVA\nabout same value as Q computed at transformer
TEXT 240 552 Left 2 ;Transformer nominal power = 300MVA\nux=0.2 therefore max Q = 300MVA/ux=1500MVA=1.5GVA\nThis is nearly the same value as on the qmeter device
TEXT 160 152 Left 2 ;Capacitor again charging to a higher voltage\n(capacitive inrush)\ntherefore is the current at 3.2s higher
TEXT -224 104 Left 2 ;From 0s to 1.5s:\nThe reactive power of the network is about -220MVAr\nThis is the reactive power of the line capacitances\n \nFrom 1.5s to 3.2s:\nThe reactive power goes from -220MVAr to +1200MVar\nThis is about 1420MVar difference\nThis is due to the inductive reacitve power consume\nof the shorted transformer.
